[interviewer · RECOMMENDATION · 1:57] Understood. What is the biggest risk to that recommendation, and how would you mitigate it?

[candidate · 2:04] The biggest risk is demand elasticity on the price move. Same-store volume growth of 15% is the only thing currently holding this business up — it's what absorbed a large part of the 38-point shock and kept the decline to 18 points on the statement. If a 10-12% increase on a menu that hasn't moved in two years triggers a 10% traffic drop, I've traded the one healthy part of the P&L for the fix, and net I'm no better off.

